==German==

===Etymology===
{{compound|ost|Deutschland|lang=de|gloss1=east|gloss2=Germany}}.

===Proper noun===
{{head|de|proper noun|g=n}}

# {{historical|lang=de}} [[eastern]] [[Germany]], Germany east of the Elbe
# [[East Germany]], the former German Democratic Republic

====Usage notes====
* While geographically not completely accurate (some parts of the former West Germany are located further east than parts of the former East Germany), this term is frequently used in German, as in English, to distinguish the region formerly known as "East Germany" or German Democratic Republic (Deutsche Demokratische Republik) from the former "West Germany" or Federal Republic of Germany (Bundesrepublik Deutschland), which were separate from 1949 until they were reunified in 1990 as the Federal Republic of Germany.

